<!-- ── II. Devotional ────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
<section class="lp-band lp-band--cream">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="lp-split">
      <div class="lp-plate lp-plate--art">
        <img src="{{asset "images/tfr/vermeer-martha-mary.jpg"}}" alt="" loading="lazy" />
      </div>
      <div class="lp-split-text">
        <p class="lp-num">Devotional</p>
        <h2 class="lp-head">The tradition was written to be used.</h2>
        <p class="lp-body">Most of what the church wrote across two thousand years was meant for use rather than for the archive: catechisms written to teach children, confessions drawn up by congregations under pressure, prayers set down for people who did not know what to say. Read a question or a page at a time, they steady a faith that has gone thin. The people who wrote them had been through what you are going through.</p>
        <a href="/the-faith-received/library/" class="btn btn-primary">Start reading</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ── III. The corpus in numbers ────────────────────────────────── -->
